# AFTER STUDIE II / five-tone tape apparatus / original procedural miniature.
# Reference: the instrument-construction research of Antonio de Sousa Dias.
# https://github.com/asousadias/Stockhausen_ElektronischStudie2_1954
# This is NOT his score excerpt and NOT a complete reconstruction of Studie II.
# Frequencies derive independently from 100 * 5^(k/25); five mixture widths.
# Five 55.5 ms sine slices excite a reverb; every dry slice ends at 277.5 ms.
# Each output contour remains exactly ZERO through at least 350 ms.
# Consequently only the chamber tail is heard. Reverb is the material, not decoration.
# syNo r9 uses its existing synthetic 6.65 s stereo IR, not the historical 10 s chamber.
# New onsets, envelopes and object order below are composed for this syNo miniature.
# Loop OFF. Source/provenance: docs/historical-studies.md.

# Exact absolute-frequency table: one definition, one-based n positions.
